eachable and differs from Jira'","differ.py:591-597 — a field enters `changed` only when local_val != jira_val; for non-FIELD_CLASSES fields resolved=local_val, for state fields resolved=local_val (local wins), so an empty-local reachable field resolves to None which still differs from jira","AC1 requires the (outbound,update) empty-effective-payload count to be 0 down from ~516"],"finding":"The plan asserts the ~516 empty-local_fields branch-3 mutations are inert and that AC1 drives them to 0, but by the plan's own survival rule any Jira-reachable field (summary/status/etc.) whose resolved value differs from jira is EMITTED — including the 'local empty, jira has summary -> resolved None emitted' case the plan itself gives. The plan never states why the 516 contain ONLY non-reachable (EXCLUDED/bookkeeping/labels-only) differing fields, which is the load-bearing fact connecting the mechanism to AC1=0.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc9aca82c74383e80","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Why / Acceptance Criteria AC1","norm_id":"nb4e246a64db2aaf4","priority":0.5211,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A both-branch key whose only differing fields are reachable scalars would be EMITTED by the new rule, so the 516 cannot all be reachable if AC1=0 is to hold — the plan must be relying on the 516 being non-reachable-only diffs"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Mitigate the duplicated Jira-reachable field list: either derive it from a single shared constant/predicate (importable without pulling batch_dispatch's side effects) or add an AC / test that fails if the differ's inline set diverges from the dispatch path's accepted fields.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e"],"criteria":["T5e"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'retain only fields accepted by the existing Jira update path (summary, description, assignee, priority, status) plus dedicated routed fields ... (parent, reporter; see dispatch_apply_phases.py and dispatch_one.py)'","The accepted-field set is the source of truth in a different module; inline duplication couples differ.py to it without an interface boundary."],"finding":"The plan chooses to compute the Jira-reachable field list inline in differ.py (explicitly avoiding a batch_dispatch import), hardcoding the set {summary, description, assignee, priority, status, parent, reporter}. This duplicates knowledge that actually lives in dispatch_apply_phases.py / dispatch_one.py; if that set changes there, the differ's inline list drifts silently — re-emitting inert mutations, or worse, dropping genuine ones.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4358f8a42b39ea66","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section: 'compute the survival test inline in differ.py (no batch_dispatch import)'","norm_id":"nf9462d6be3e909d2","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future ticket adds a new Jira-reachable scalar field to dispatch_one.py but not to the differ's inline list — the differ drops that field's mutation as 'inert', silently losing a real Jira update."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Extract the Jira-reachable field set into a shared constant (e.g. a module-level frozenset in a low-dependency module) that both differ.py and the dispatch path reference, and add a unit test asserting the two stay in sync.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Justify or eliminate the duplication of `_OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST` in differ.py: either import/share the single source-of-truth constant, or add a test that asserts differ.py's inline field set stays equal to `_OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST` (plus the routed {parent, reporter}) so drift is caught.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["dispatch_apply_phases.py:73 `_OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST = frozenset({\"summary\", \"description\", \"assignee\", \"priority\", \"status\"})` — the plan's field list is an exact copy","dispatch_apply_phases.py:301,308 and dispatch_one.py:501 (`_update_one_filter_fields`) show this frozenset is the authoritative filter that determines what survives to update_issue","The in-code comment at dispatch_apply_phases.py:69-72 documents `status` was added later by bug 85a1 — evidence the set is a moving target, so a hardcoded copy will drift"],"finding":"The plan hardcodes the Jira-reachable scalar field set {summary, description, assignee, priority, status} inline in differ.py, which is a verbatim copy of the existing single-source-of-truth `_OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST` frozenset (dispatch_apply_phases.py:73). Duplicating this constant risks silent divergence: the allowlist has changed before (bug 85a1 added `status`), and any future add/remove would leave differ.py's inert-detection out of sync, causing it to either drop genuine mutations or re-admit inert ones.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fff588bca91ed020a","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Approach' ('retain only fields accepted by the existing Jira update path (summary, description, assignee, priority, status)')","norm_id":"ne791262a19408a05","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future ticket adds a field to _OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST (e.g. duedate); differ.py's inline copy is not updated and now wrongly classifies a real duedate-only update as inert, silently dropping it","A field is removed from the allowlist for a Jira-endpoint reason; differ.py keeps emitting mutations that the applier will strip — reintroducing the exact inert-mutation waste this plan removes"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State in the Approach how the two field lists are kept in sync — e.g. add an equivalence assertion test (differ's inert-field set == `_OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST` | {parent, reporter}) so a future edit to the dispatch allowlist fails loudly rather than diverging silently.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Guard against allowlist drift: either add a unit assertion that the differ's inline reachable-scalar set equals dispatch_apply_phases._OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST (plus the routed {parent,reporter}), or justify in the plan why the differ purity constraint outweighs the drift risk and how future edits will be kept in sync.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'retain only fields accepted by the existing Jira update path (summary, description, assignee, priority, status) ... compute the survival test inline in differ.py (no batch_dispatch import)'","dispatch_apply_phases.py:73 _OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST = frozenset({'summary','description','assignee','priority','status'}) is the live source the differ copy must track"],"finding":"The plan inlines a hand-copied reachable-scalar set {summary,description,assignee,priority,status} in differ.py to avoid a batch_dispatch import, but this silently duplicates _OUTBOUND_BATCH_ALLOWLIST (dispatch_apply_phases.py:73) with no shared source-of-truth and no test coupling the two — so a future change to the dispatch allowlist re-introduces inert mutations (a field added to dispatch but not the differ copy) or drops genuine payloads (a field removed).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f254002f6a5a8cf23","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach","norm_id":"nf5e89130e3f39efd","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A later ticket adds a sixth allowlisted scalar to the dispatch path; the differ's frozen inline copy keeps skipping it, re-introducing exactly the inert-emission class this ticket removes but in the opposite direction (a genuine field is now treated as non-reachable and dropped)"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"38a675cd1cb6f32b","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["f95b5918e6a16528",3285],"description_boxes":["1a0f564ddc603945",0],"file_impact":["9e1ecd8b39f8